// ── node_build_bottom_up(entries, lo, hi, depth) -> HamtNode ─────────────────
// Direct bottom-up HAMT construction from a dense range of HamtEntry structs
// (spike). Counting-sorts [lo,hi) by the depth's 5-bit hash fragment into a
// fresh per-node scratch array, then allocates each node's bitmap + exact-sized
// entries array once. Slot rule: a singleton bucket becomes a leaf HamtEntry; a
// multi-entry bucket at depth >= 12 (all 64 hash bits consumed, so a genuine
// full-hash collision) becomes a HamtCollision; otherwise recurse at depth+1.
// This matches node_set's structure exactly while touching each entry O(depth)
// times instead of doing one full hash/trie traversal per entry.
//
// Naive form: allocates fresh count/cursor/scratch arrays per node rather than
// ping-ponging a shared scratch buffer. Caller guarantees hi > lo.
fn node_build_bottom_up_fn() FuncDef {
  // p0=entries, p1=lo, p2=hi, p3=depth
  // L4=n, L5=shift(i64), L6=counts, L7=cur, L8=sorted, L9=i, L10=f,
  // L11=bitmap, L12=acc, L13=entry, L14=hash, L15=nslots, L16=slots, L17=si,
  // L18=base, L19=c, L20=pos, L21=bucket
